  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 336 PM EDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\n===== Drier Trend This Weekend, But Hotter Temperatures =====\n\nUpper ridging will build across the US over the weekend, leading to \na drier trend for our area. However, this will also lead to much \nhotter temps, with daily highs in the 90s both days. With dewpoints \nreaching the mid 70s, that will easily yield heat indices between \n105-110 both Saturday and Sunday. There is high confidence that \nwe'll need a heat headline for the weekend. \n\n===== Precip Chances Return Early Next Week =====\n\nA frontal boundary will shift southward through the Ohio Valley \nSunday night and into Monday, and will likely bring a round of \nshowers and storms to the area. Any overnight convection Sunday \nnight will be elevated, but redevelopment Monday afternoon would be \nsfc based in a highly unstable airmass. Not a lot of shear expected \nthen to limit organization, but certainly could see scattered \nthunderstorms on Monday. \n\nTuesday and Wednesday appear mostly dry, with mainly isolated chances \neast of I-65 both days. Sfc high pressure will be centered to our \nnorth then, so not going to expect much activity for the mid-week.",
